      "text": "Freshwater covers less than 1% of Earth's surface and holds only 0.01% of its water, yet supports ~10% of all described species and provides drinking water, food, and water regulation for billions of people. Limnology (the science of inland waters) spans physical, chemical, and biological dimensions across four habitat types: lakes, rivers, wetlands, and groundwater."
